{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040161-host-jump-and-ghosts","id":1040161,"title":"Host jump and ghosts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-29T13:01:12-08:00","id":1040161,"title":"Host jump and ghosts","content":"Hello, <br /> <br /> I try to create a &quot;host jumping ghost&quot; for my chronicle. Actually I find the rules quite hard to understand, so I hope I did everything correctly so far...<br /> I think, the ghost needs to be Rank 4 to be able to match all the prerequisites for &quot;Host Jump&quot;, if I am not mistaken!?<br /> <br /> Host Jump:<br /> The entity may leap from host to host when using the Possess or Claim Manifestations. <br /> 1. The current host must touch the intended host while the entity spends 3 Essence, and the new host must be under any prerequisite Conditions. <br /> 2. If both prerequisites are met, the entity immediately transfers the Possessed or Claimed Condition to the new host, although Claimed must begin the process of Claiming again. <br /> 3. The entity does not need to re-spend Essence on the Manifestation Effect when jumping hosts with this Numen. <br /> <br /> --------------------------<br /> Process of Claiming??<br /> --------------------------<br /> <br /> Claim (Requires Rank 3)<br /> 1. Requires Controlled Condition<br /> 2. Spending 5 Essence (the entity gains permanent control over an object, creature or corpse, applying the Claimed Condition to the subject).<br /> 3. Power + Finesse VS Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance <br /> <br /> Influence Effect: Control<br /> 1. This Infuence can shift the Open Condition to Controlled for its duration. <br /> 2. The cost is 3 Essence. <br /> <br /> Influence Effect: Strengthen<br /> 1. This Infuence can shift the Anchor, Resonant or Infrastructure Condition to Open for its duration. <br /> 2. The cost is 1 Essence. <br /> <br /> Influence Effect: Create (Requires Rank 4)<br /> 1. The entity can ... create a new anchor ... The entity can cause a temporary Anchor ... in a subject for the duration of the Influence. <br /> 2. The cost is 4 Essence. <br /> --------------------------<br /> <br /> Question 1: <br /> Is the list above the &quot;process of Claiming&quot;?<br /> <br /> Question 2:<br /> The only manifestation effect in the list is claimed. So does this mean, the ghost still needs 11 essence and a contested roll for every attempt to &quot;jump&quot;? And does the ghost loose 8 essence, if it fails, during the &quot;process of Claiming&quot;?<br /> <br /> Question 3:<br /> Is there a cheaper way to achieve more or less the same? Something a Rank 2 ghost could manage?<br /> <br /> Question 4:<br /> Is there a limit to the number of anchors a ghost can create? <br /> <br /> Question 5:<br /> How can a group of humans exorcise the ghost, if the anchors are living persons? Or is there also another way to deal with it? I mean, even if exorcised, what's keeping it from coming back? How can they &quot;defeat&quot; it? <br /> (I am considering to change a character into a sin-eater at the moment. I read that they are able to destroy ghosts somehow... <br /> And the group already knows, that they might not stay human during the chronicle.)<br /> <br /> Question 6:<br /> When a ghost looses all anchors, how do I decide, if the ghost &quot;passes on&quot; or is sent to the Underworld?<br /> <br /> Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":1825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","user":"Elythia","date":". 01-29-2017, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:21:39-08:00","id":1040173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040161-host-jump-and-ghosts#post1040161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question 3:<br /> Is there a cheaper way to achieve more or less the same? Something a Rank 2 ghost could manage?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd want to hinge it on Possess, not Claim. There's an entity in werewolf called the Nanutari, or Spirit Thieves, that basically do this. Claiming is more for long term symbiosis, it would create a lot of body warping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:55:49-08:00","id":1040197,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the reply! Maybe I need to explain in more detail, what I want to achieve:<br /> <br /> I got inspired by the book &quot;What the night knows&quot; by Dean Koontz. <br /> <br /> (Spoiler alert!)<br /> <br /> In short it is about a serial killer named &quot;Alton Turner Blackwood&quot;, who killes families in a ritualistic way and tries to send them as his slaves to hell for later. He has also a strange connection to a raven, who teaches him everything about the night before he goes on his killing spree.. At a certain point Blackwood starts to believe that he has become an aspect of death itself.<br /> <br /> In the book the main character shoots Blackwood, when he returns home and finds his family dead. He was 15 years old or something like that. Years later, the character is married and has three children of his own. At this point Blackwood returns as a &quot;host jumper&quot;. The book mentions that he is now supported by a demon, but not how.<br /> <br /> The main character became a homicide detective and is really pussled, since the murders seem almost identical to those of Blackwood. Even the relationship of the family members are similar. Only the ritual is missing this time.<br /> As a &quot;host jumper&quot; (the book calls it rider) Blackwood needs quite some time to find his new victims and arrange everything ahead. He has a fixed schedule of 33 days between each family. Furthermore all of his &quot;claimed&quot;(?) persons, that he uses, are aware of what is going on, but usually can't fight it. &quot;Possessed&quot; persons are also kind of asleep, I believe. He can also switch to things, not only persons.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> At the moment the group is playing characters at the police that investigates the murder of the first family. Blackwood is at this point still a human antagonist. <br /> The ghost (the word is never used in the book..) in the original story has around 20 years, I believe, before it returns. To keep it playable my version of Blackwood has only a few weeks or month before that happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":1825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","user":"Elythia","date":". 01-29-2017, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T18:09:04-08:00","id":1040332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040161-host-jump-and-ghosts?p=1040197#post1040197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short it is about a serial killer named &quot;Alton Turner Blackwood&quot;, who killes families in a ritualistic way and tries to send them as his slaves to hell for later. He has also a strange connection to a raven, who teaches him everything about the night before he goes on his killing spree.. At a certain point Blackwood starts to believe that he has become an aspect of death itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the book the main character shoots Blackwood, when he returns home and finds his family dead. He was 15 years old or something like that. Years later, the character is married and has three children of his own. At this point Blackwood returns as a &quot;host jumper&quot;. The book mentions that he is now supported by a demon, but not how.[/quote]<br /> <br /> With this kind of thing you have ample justification to bend the rules as they exist. As he's being patroned by a demon, the ghost may have access to Manifestations that don't quite act like existing ones, for instance allowing him to Possess for longer periods of time and keeping the host 'aware.' You can always do this sort of thing, change the rules to fit your game, but it dovetails nicely with a in-world justification in this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The main character became a homicide detective and is really pussled, since the murders seem almost identical to those of Blackwood. Even the relationship of the family members are similar. Only the ritual is missing this time.<br /> As a &quot;host jumper&quot; (the book calls it rider) Blackwood needs quite some time to find his new victims and arrange everything ahead. He has a fixed schedule of 33 days between each family. Furthermore all of his &quot;claimed&quot;(?) persons, that he uses, are aware of what is going on, but usually can't fight it. &quot;Possessed&quot; persons are also kind of asleep, I believe. He can also switch to things, not only persons. </div> </div> </div>They are basically asleep, but you could have it so that they're slightly aware, maybe if the host is forced to do something that would be a Breaking Point, they can spend a Willpower to try and resist or take control long enough to say something, perhaps warning a loved one about to get the axe.<br /> <br /> At the moment the group is playing characters at the police that investigates the murder of the first family. Blackwood is at this point still a human antagonist.<br /> The ghost (the word is never used in the book..) in the original story has around 20 years, I believe, before it returns. To keep it playable my version of Blackwood has only a few weeks or month before that happens.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> So he is a ghost in the book?<br /> <br /> It sounds like the ritual he performs would allow him to Fetter himself to the target family, or turn them into his anchor, which would allow him to Possess or Claim them, or possibly things associated with them, like the family's home. Alternatively the object manipulation could be done through something like Left-Handed Spanner or Telekinesis, so you could keep the ghost 'purely' a host jumper.<br /> <br /> I wanted to hit your original questions, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Question 1: <br /> Is the list above the &quot;process of Claiming&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Mechanically, yes. There are story ways it can happen. Idigam, for instance, can make things Claim others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Question 2:<br /> The only manifestation effect in the list is claimed. So does this mean, the ghost still needs 11 essence and a contested roll for every attempt to &quot;jump&quot;? And does the ghost loose 8 essence, if it fails, during the &quot;process of Claiming&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Hmm. It looks like with Host Jump you don't need a new roll to do the Claiming, but you might need it to build up the necessary Conditions. I do believe you can sort of skip using Controlled-to-Open. The book says it involves the subject and entity acting in concert for a series of turns, I guess it primes the way between them. Rituals could do this sort of thing, too, certain rituals would do the same thing. It's how mortal spiritualists who can't do the Influence stuff manage to deal with spirits and ghosts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Question 4:<br /> Is there a limit to the number of anchors a ghost can create? </div> </div> </div>Just the ghost's capability, there doesn't seem to be any hard rule on anchor limits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Question 5:<br /> How can a group of humans exorcise the ghost, if the anchors are living persons? Or is there also another way to deal with it? I mean, even if exorcised, what's keeping it from coming back? How can they &quot;defeat&quot; it? </div> </div> </div>In the God-Machine book, there's some rules for Exorcism and Abjuration. An Exorcism basically finds ways to remove the underlying Conditions, like Anchor, without necessarily killing the ghost. A son may 'get over' their father's death and forgive them for their sins in life, for instance. Abjuration is more supernatural, sort of like the little woman from Poltergeist or the one from Insidious, someone using their sheer Resolve and virtue to knock the Manifestations from a ghost.<br /> <br /> Generally to finally kill things like these, you need to destroy them when they have no power left. So fill all their Corpus boxes with Lethal damage while also draining them of Essence. It's easiest to do this through use of bans and banes if you don't have magical powers yourself. But for story purposes, just getting rid of a ghost's anchors will usually send it to the Underworld. While its return is possible, it's not always guaranteed, as the Underworld doesn't really like to let go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Question 6:<br /> When a ghost looses all anchors, how do I decide, if the ghost &quot;passes on&quot; or is sent to the Underworld? </div> </div> </div>It's a story thing. Mechanically, like I said above, a ghost is fully destroyed if it's full of damage and has no Essence left, meaning it can't reform even in the Underworld. But just losing its anchors would likely make it go to the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T11:04:19-08:00","id":1040772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1040161-host-jump-and-ghosts?p=1040332#post1040332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So he is a ghost in the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>The book is written from the humans point of view. They know he is back at some point, but they don't know how he came back nor as &quot;what&quot; he came back. <br /> <br /> (Question 5)<br /> As far as I understand it, they need to create a new anchor for every new host. Since these aren't &quot;natural&quot; anchors like the ones you get after dying, they are lacking any other connection to the ghost. They ghost isn't someone they knew, he just decided to create an anchor. <br /> (Spoiler) <br /> Hm, considering the book at this point, all the &quot;old&quot; hosts died in one way or another. <br /> --<br /> I read about exorcism and those things, but I still find it hard to put it into practice:<br /> How does a human even find a ghost or a possessed human in the first place? <br /> How do they find out possible bans and banes about someone who just became a ghost!?<br /> And how do they prevent him from &quot;jumping&quot; to someone or something at sight before &quot;starting&quot;? Or simply leaving into Twilight? <br /> Actually I find it quite hard to imagine, that an exorcism by humans can be successful, if the ghost is not staying anywhere close to his &quot;natural&quot; anchors.<br /> <br /> At the moment I believe the best answer, to handle these difficulties, are sin-eaters. They can recognize possessed or claimed humans, see them, if the &quot;jump&quot; or &quot;leave&quot; and handle them. Only the problem of finding the current host would remain. -&gt; Any suggestions are welcome!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Furthermore I found an interesting passage in the book:<br /> &quot;A Sin-Eater can also directly target a ghost that possesses someone by attacking it in Twilight without causing damage to the host.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":1825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","user":"Elythia","date":". 01-30-2017, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}